cabal-version:   3.0
name:            clientsession
version:         0.9.3.0
synopsis:        Compile-only stand-in for clientsession on wasm32-wasi
description:
  This is the one genuinely fictional shim in this project, and the reason the
  PoC's Yesod applications must not use client sessions.
  .
  The real package encrypts session cookies with AES-CTR and authenticates them
  with Skein-MAC-512-256, via `crypton` -> `memory` -> `basement`, none of which
  builds for wasm32-wasi. `yesod-core` depends on it unconditionally, even for an
  application that never opens a session.
  .
  Every cryptographic operation here raises an error describing the situation.
  An application that sets @makeSessionBackend _ = pure Nothing@ never reaches
  them; one that uses sessions will fail at runtime rather than at compile time,
  which is the cost of this approach.

license:         BSD-3-Clause
author:          workers-wai PoC
build-type:      Simple

library
  hs-source-dirs:   src
  exposed-modules:  Web.ClientSession
  build-depends:
    , base        >=4.17 && <5
    , bytestring

  default-language: Haskell2010
  ghc-options:      -Wall
